From 96d554aa9d83f89124bd99e188c8f5b21d60a031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:12:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/56] demux: dash: report success once the meta has been
 filled in

DEMUX_GET_META builds the metadata, merges it into the caller vlc_meta_t
and then breaks out of the switch into
PlaylistManager::doControl(i_query, args). That has no case for this
query, so it falls to its default and returns VLC_EGENERIC: the metadata
is there but the caller is told the request failed.

The forwarded args has also already been walked by the va_arg above, so
the call is passed a va_list in a state it does not expect.

Return success from the branch that produced the metadata. The paths that
produce none are left to fall through as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/dash/DASHManager.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/dash/DASHManager.cpp b/modules/demux/dash/DASHManager.cpp
index 687794f7b9..0950b3a4ad 100644
--- a/modules/demux/dash/DASHManager.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/dash/DASHManager.cpp
@@ -163,7 +163,12 @@ int DASHManager::doControl(int i_query, va_list args)
 
             vlc_meta_Merge(p_meta, meta);
             vlc_meta_Delete(meta);
-            break;
+            /* The meta has been filled in, so report that rather than falling
+             * through: PlaylistManager::doControl() has no case for this query
+             * and answers VLC_EGENERIC, which told the caller nothing had been
+             * produced. It would also be handed an args that has already been
+             * walked. */
+            return VLC_SUCCESS;
         }
     }
     return PlaylistManager::doControl(i_query, args);
